
==== 1  the scenario: how many collisions per bunch crossing =========================================
  Run 3 (2024, levelled): L = 2.00e+34 cm^-2 s^-1, sigma_inel = 78.42 mb (PYTHIA, CP5, the tune fixes it),
  n_b = 2350 colliding bunches, f_rev = 11245.5 Hz: 1.568e+09 collisions/s over 2.643e+07 crossings/s
  mu = L sigma / (n_b f_rev) = 59.3 (60.5 with the 80 mb of the bookkeeping); the mixing scenario rounds it to mu = 60 (CMSSW AVE_60_BX_25ns), window bx = -12 ... +3, 960 collisions expected per signal event
  the Run-3 production mixes Run3_Flat55To75_PoissonOOTPU: mu_true of the in-time crossing drawn flat in 55 ... 75 (mean 65), Poisson draws of the same mean in the other 15 crossings, about 1040 collisions per signal event; this record fixes mu_true = 60

==== 2  the draw of the MixingModule: Poisson(mu) collisions per bunch crossing ======================
  bx -12: 60, bx -11: 56, bx -10: 68, bx -9: 61, bx -8: 66, bx -7: 56, bx -6: 55, bx -5: 50, bx -4: 53, bx -3: 66, bx -2: 61, bx -1: 60, bx +0: 63, bx +1: 63, bx +2: 59, bx +3: 63; 960 collisions for an expectation of 960 (Poisson: 60 +- 7.7 per crossing)
  library: 2000 events, read at random positions, with replacement; 763 distinct events used
  process types: CD 16, DD 115, ND 667, SD 162 (library shares: CD 1.9%, DD 10.9%, ND 71.2%, SD 15.9%)

==== 3  the beam spot: where and when each collision happens =========================================
  BetafuncEvtVtxGenerator with the 2024 payload (SimBeamSpot_Realistic25ns13p6TeVEarly2024CollisionVtxSmearingParameters_v1_mc):
  centre (0.0285, -0.0166, 0.416) cm, sigma_z = 3.6 cm, beta* = 30 cm, emittance 5.725e-08 cm: sigma_xy = 9.3 um at the focus, x sqrt(1 + ((z - z0)/beta*)^2) away from it (the hourglass)
  sigma_z, sigma_t of the model: 3.60 cm, 120 ps (sigma_t = sigma_z / c, z and t independent: what two head-on Gaussian bunches of 5.1 cm would give; the payload is a fit to the 2024 data, the crossing angle folded in)
  drawn: 960 vertices with r.m.s. x 9.2 um, y 9.4 um, z 3.79 cm (mean 0.28), t 119 ps; z from -12.4 to 13.9 cm
  the signal vertex: x = 285.9 um, y = -164.1 um, z = -0.17 cm, t = -121 ps; the out-of-time crossings are shifted by 25 ns x bx (the CMSSW signal event of the companion sits at z = 3.11 cm, t = -140 ps)

==== 4  the stacking: one final state out of the signal and the in-time crowd ========================
  the signal: 744 final particles without the neutrinos, 651 within |eta| < 5
  in-time (bx = 0): 63 collisions, 12113 final particles, 9033 within |eta| < 5 and not neutrinos; the mixed final state has 9684 particles
  particles per crossing: bx -12: 10815, bx -11: 9137, bx -10: 14169, bx -9: 10920, bx -8: 11455, bx -7: 10482, bx -6: 10417, bx -5: 7385, bx -4: 8901, bx -3: 13258, bx -2: 10255, bx -1: 11492, bx +0: 12113, bx +1: 12250, bx +2: 10265, bx +3: 10144; the out-of-time ones are recorded with their time offset and not clustered
  the in-time crowd in the tracker (|eta| < 2.5, pT > 0.5): 860 charged particles against 93 of the signal

==== 5  anti-kT on the mixed final state, with ghosts for the areas ==================================
  9684 particles + 6300 ghosts of area 0.0100 (|y| < 5): 15984 steps in 117 s; 173 jets above 3 GeV, 62 above 30
  the b jet: chapter-7 jet [0] 99.83 GeV, 31 particles -> mixed jet [0] 132.75 GeV, 112 particles (31 signal, 81 pileup from 34 collisions), dR = 0.042, area 0.529 (pi R^2 = 0.503); signal pT inside 100.07, pileup pT inside 33.61
    of the 31 particles of the photograph 31 are in the mixed jet, 0 fell out, 0 signal particles joined
  the bbar jet: chapter-7 jet [1] 94.09 GeV, 18 particles -> mixed jet [1] 124.71 GeV, 98 particles (18 signal, 80 pileup from 36 collisions), dR = 0.022, area 0.499 (pi R^2 = 0.503); signal pT inside 94.30, pileup pT inside 31.26

==== 6  the median energy density rho, two ways ======================================================
  grid median (fixedGridRhoFastjetAll): 18 x 11 cells of 0.556 x 0.571 = 0.317 in |y| < 5, phi from 0; rho = 68.28 GeV per unit area (cells from 13.4 to 358.5, mean 73.96)
  the same grid on the signal alone: rho = 3.42 (the underlying event of chapter 4, and nothing in most cells)
  jet median (Cacciari-Salam): kT jets of R = 0.4 with ghosts, 197 jets, 175 within |y| < 4.4; rho = 69.87 GeV per unit area (pT/A from 30.3 to 297.4); 18 s
  per collision: 1.084 (grid) and 1.109 (jets) GeV per unit area

