==== 8  the vertices the tracker will see ============================================================
  in-time collisions with >= 4 charged particles of pT > 0.5 GeV within |eta| < 2.5: 43 of 63 (68%); CMS reconstructs about 0.7 mu primary vertices
  the nearest crowd vertex to the signal's: 0.06 mm away in z, 5 ps in t; 4 within 1 mm (the vertex finder's reach), 7 within 30 ps (what the timing layer of Phase 2 would resolve; Run 3 has none)

==== 9  the pileup profile of a fill, and the reweighting ============================================
  a 2024-like fill (levelled at mu = 60 for 8 h, then decaying with tau = 10 h, 12 h in all): mu from 40 to 60, luminosity-weighted mean 57, 72% of the collisions at the levelled value
  a 2024-like year of such fills levelled between 57 and 67: mean 59, 68% of the collisions between 52 and 66 (a model; the measured profile is what an analysis reweights to)
  the production's flat profile (probFunction, mu_true uniform in 55 ... 75): the weight w = P_2024(mu_true) / P_flat(mu_true) runs from 0.00 to 1.62 over the flat range, 1.54 at mu_true = 60
  a sample mixed at a fixed mu = 60 reweighted to the same profile: w = 0.07 for every event, and no event at all for the rest of the profile; the flat profile costs events at the edges and covers the whole year
  for comparison a levelled HL-LHC fill (mu = 200 for 8 h, then tau = 5 h, 12 h): mean 186, 75% of the collisions at the levelled value
